{
  "id": "01-the-old-life",
  "title": "Lay Down the Old Life",
  "tenet": "Let the flesh lose its rule",
  "durationMs": 44088,
  "audioAsset": "kingdom/01-the-old-life.mp3",
  "transcriptAsset": "assets/kingdom/01-the-old-life.json",
  "text": "A child once watched his father mend a broken gate. The father did not paint over the rust. He took away the damaged hinge, set a new one in place, and taught his son how to keep it strong. Our habits can be like that gate. The animal impulses in us demand comfort, control, and the last word. Jesus calls us to lay down that old rule. Dying to the flesh is not hatred of the body. It is refusing to let appetite, fear, or pride command the heart. Bring one stubborn impulse into the light today. Ask Christ for mercy. Then practice one concrete act of self control, with help when you need it. The new life begins in surrender, and grows through faithful choices.",
